{
  "k": 3,
  "repository": "cobra",
  "vendored": "benchmarks/corpus/cobra",
  "why": "The third graded repository, and the first that is not Python. Four constants -- `search.min_coverage`, `search.min_concentration`, `COMMON_TERM` and `COVERAGE_FULL_STRENGTH` -- were fitted on two corpora that a single author wrote or chose, both Python, both with documentation *inside* the declaration. Go writes it above, outside the unit's span, so this ruler grades the line-scanner path and the rule table rather than the AST path, on prose the parser has to pick up rather than read out of a syntax tree.",
  "caveat": "Twenty subjects, each asked in English and in Chinese, phrased in a user's words rather than in the words of the doc comment that answers them. Forty questions is a smaller instrument than the seventy in repo_queries.json; it resolves a change of several questions, not of one. Every acceptable answer is checked against the index before anything is scored.",
  "measured_against": {
    "upstream": "https://github.com/spf13/cobra",
    "tag": "v1.9.1",
    "commit": "40b5bc1437a564fc795d388b23835e84f54cd1d1",
    "released": "2025-02-16",
    "licence": "Apache-2.0, carried at benchmarks/corpus/cobra/LICENSE.txt",
    "omitted": "site/, assets/ and .git/; every .go file at that tag is present byte for byte",
    "note": "Chosen by measuring three candidates against the subject words of benchmarks/absent_queries.json: cobra collides on eight ordinary English words, chi on eighteen and gin on seventeen including `oauth`, `codec` and `hostname`. Rebuild with `rag-your-code index benchmarks/corpus/cobra`."
  },
